# nav.pdl - how an agent (or a presentation script) DRIVES Deskopoly inside the rpg-edit-hq editor, fast and without guessing (2026-11-08; every row was learned by driving the real window).
# Format:  NAV | kind | name | value | note        (data only; the executable form is tests/*.pdl, run by `relay_drive <pid> run <script> <winid>`)
# Source of truth for what is on screen: the window's OWN text dump, #.desktop/ascii_frames/<pid>.<seq>.objects.pdl (highest seq of OUR pid): one line per object with id, x y w h, nav, label.
# Never keep a pixel or nav-number table: nav numbers shift (the popup's first button is nav 22 in setup, 27 in play, 37 with the Player menu open); ids and labels do not.

# ---- the protocol (each row is a mistake that cost a run) ----
NAV | protocol | leave-in      | key esc                          | with In: ON the editor sends keys to the game world, so typed nav digits do not navigate; ONE Esc leaves In (more are harmless)
NAV | protocol | gentle        | RELAY_DRIVE_NO_ESC=1             | relay_drive's own Esc flips In: and closes an open dropdown, and its 'p' key is typed into an open dropdown's search; gentle mode reads the objects dump instead
NAV | protocol | menu-rows     | tapid pm-*                       | Player-menu rows react to a mouse click, not to Enter (Enter closes the menu without firing the row)
NAV | protocol | popup-buttons | press label:<text>               | the popup buttons (gmb0..) react to nav digits + Enter; label match is "first CLICKABLE element whose label contains the text" (gentle mode)
NAV | protocol | tap-once      | verify in the ledger, then retry | a focused button activates on ONE tap; a blind double tap pressed Roll and then End turn (the list changes under your finger)
NAV | protocol | sync          | the LEDGER, not the popup text   | at fast speed the pets overwrite the popup message within a moment; the ledger cannot be overwritten
NAV | protocol | step-fields    | no bar inside a STEP field       | a STEP row splits on the bar character, so expectations hold no bar (use next=p2;round=3, bought-150, total=2)
NAV | protocol | start-state   | deskopoly_ctl new_game, setup_reset | setup choices (seat, speed) persist across New game; setup_reset gives 3 players, no seat, seed 7, normal speed
NAV | protocol | restore       | press tb-in                      | the harness leaves In: off after the Esc; press tb-in once at the end to hand the editor back as found (default is ON)
NAV | protocol | see           | STEP see <id or label:text> [absent] | asserts what is ON SCREEN from the window's own objects dump (any object, clickable or not; polls 5 s). Data checks cannot see a screen that is not drawn: pt0..ptN (players bar), gme0 (footer), label:TEROPOLY (popup) exist only while a game runs
NAV | protocol | ensure        | STEP ensure <target> <opener>       | presses the opener ONLY when the target is not clickable yet (a blind press on tb-player CLOSES an open Player menu)
NAV | protocol | in            | STEP in on or off                    | sets In: only if needed; turning it off uses ONE Esc because nav digits go to the game world while In is ON; In: ON also PAUSES the game clock (rpg.pdl running=0)
NAV | script   | dsk-open-play | tests/dsk-open-play.pdl             | from any editor state to Play pressed (in off, ensure menu, tapid pm-play); tests/dsk-in-on.pdl hands the editor back

# ---- stable ids (resolve at run time from the dump) ----
NAV | id | tb-in        | In: ON/off toggle                         | toolbar tab
NAV | id | tb-player    | Player menu (opens the dropdown)          | toolbar tab, "Player: playing/stopped"
NAV | id | pm-play      | Player > Play                             | starts the book's driver (deskopoly_driver); tapid
NAV | id | pm-stop      | Player > Stop                             | freezes the game (the ledger stops growing); tapid
NAV | id | pm-cancel    | Player > - cancel -                       | closes the menu
NAV | id | gmb0..gmbN   | the game popup buttons, top to bottom     | setup: players -, players +, you play: <none|pN>, seed N (next), speed: <fast|normal|slow>, START GAME; play: Roll | Buy <tile> (<price>) + Skip | End turn, then speed: ..., New game
NAV | id | pt0..ptN     | the players bar rows (left)               | "> p1 A $1190" = cash, current turn marked with >
NAV | id | gme0         | the footer item, all players              | ">p1 1540  p2 1490" = NET WORTH (cash is in the left bar)
NAV | id | say          | the table-talk input (right)              | TRADE COMMANDS (2026-11-08): with a game running the box is the game chat even when the chat tab says h-ai: `offer p2 give Orange3 get 20` (a tile by id OR by the label on the board: `offer p2 give 100 get Coil Plaza`; ambiguous = refused with the candidates), `counter 3 give .. get ..`, `accept`, `reject`, `cancel`, `bid 60`; `/pass` `/end` `/roll` with a slash; other lines reach the pets. Drive it with In: ON (no clock risk): relay_drive `tap 1195 396` (focuses the box), `type <text>`, `key enter` (found live 2026-11-08); the answer is in chat.txt as `game:` lines and in the popup as `chat: ...` for 6 s

# ---- scripts (tests/) ----
NAV | script | dsk-new-game   | tests/dsk-new-game.pdl   | popup New game -> setup screen
NAV | script | dsk-seat-setup | tests/dsk-seat-setup.pdl | Play, speed fast, you play p1, START GAME (24 steps incl. see assertions, 3 shots)
NAV | script | dsk-seat-turns | tests/dsk-seat-turns.pdl | three rounds as p1 with Roll / Buy / End turn (28 steps, 4 shots); seed 7 is deterministic
NAV | script | dsk-seat-trade | tests/dsk-seat-trade.pdl | on p1's turn: Trade..., press a tile (it moves into GIVE), ask 10 more x3, Send offer; the pet answers (22 steps, 4 shots); needs deskopoly_ctl with digits allowed
NAV | script | dsk-seat-auction | tests/dsk-seat-auction.pdl | right after dsk-seat-setup: Roll, End turn, Roll, SKIP on Power (seed 7) opens an auction; Bid 30, the pets raise, Pass; auction_end (28 steps, 3 shots; popup buttons Bid N / Bid N+50 / Pass are ids gmb0..)
NAV | script | dsk-stop        | tests/dsk-stop.pdl        | Player > Stop (switch running=0): the pets stop answering, so an OPEN offer stays visible; Play again with tests/dsk-open-play.pdl. WHILE STOPPED THE DRIVER WATCHDOG IS OFF: a killed driver does not come back until Play is pressed (found live 2026-11-08)
NAV | script | dsk-seat-amend | tests/dsk-seat-amend.pdl | stopped game, p1's turn: Trade..., Orange3 + ask 30, Send offer, then `Amend offer...` (screen prefilled with MY terms, `Send amendment`), ask 20, send, then `Cancel offer` (36 steps, 5 shots; run live 2026-11-08, PNGs 20-24)
NAV | script | dsk-seat-pass-turn | tests/dsk-seat-pass-turn.pdl | stopped game: Roll, Buy Yellow1, End turn (seed 7 round 4) so that p2 is the current player; a harness may then make p2 offer p1 something through the engine CLI
NAV | script | dsk-seat-counter | tests/dsk-seat-counter.pdl | stopped game, an open offer p2 -> p1: `Counter...` opens the panes with SWAPPED terms (`COUNTER to p2's offer #N`, `Send counter`), ask 10 more, send; the counter becomes MY open offer (21 steps, 4 shots; run live 2026-11-08, PNGs 30-33)
NAV | fact   | cli-offer-to-human | deskopoly.+x <book> <game dir> offer p1 give cash:20 get prop:19 as=p2, then `... ui`, then any ctl line to make the driver republish | pets cannot propose yet; while p2 is the current player in PRE this is the same verb a pet will use (dsk-seat-pass-turn.pdl leaves p2 current in a stopped game)
NAV | fact   | ctl-repeat      | env DESKOPOLY_CTL_REPEAT=<1..200> before deskopoly_ctl | a harness presses a button up to 200 times in one process (cash clamps need 93 presses); a window button never sets it. EXTRA ARGUMENTS ARE IGNORED: the khtpm renderer appends the click position (2 args) to every button action, and a positional count that refused them made every popup button dead (found live 2026-11-08)
NAV | case   | live_dsk_seat   | harness/cases/live_dsk_seat.pdl | the whole chain in the real window (LIVE_OK=1); shots land in @.apps/deskopoly/shots/ (git-ignored, wiped at the start of each run)

# ---- the overhead 3D camera (the whole 33x33 board with the extruded players) ----
# pan values are RELATIVE to the session's cam_home (it changes on every relaunch: 8 8 0 0 in one session, 16 16 60 0 in the next). Rule validated in both: pan = desired view + cam_home, field by field.
# For this board the desired view is x 8, y 8, z 9 at zoom level 12:  pan_x = 8 + home_x, pan_y = 8 + home_y, pan_z = 9 + home_z.
NAV | camera | overhead      | board_ctl camset <editor app> camera_mode=3 cam_pitch=-89 cam_yaw=180 cam_pan_x=<8+hx> cam_pan_y=<8+hy> cam_pan_z=<9+hz> cam_z_level=12 | hx hy hz = fields 1 2 3 of <bv_session>/pieces/system/cam_home.txt
NAV | camera | pitfall       | replaying a fixed key sequence (c w v) | worked in one session and showed only sky in the next, because cam_home differs
NAV | camera | 2d-view      | bv_keys <bv_session> 0                 | toggles the RPG Maker 2D view (the whole board with the walking characters) and back

# ---- facts the pictures depend on ----
NAV | fact | events-glyph    | a LETTER, never a digit                | the 3D loader reads 9 or 15 fields per events.txt row and silently drops a 10-field row (a digit glyph parses as a float): this hid every player in 3D until 2026-11-08
NAV | fact | idle-cost       | 0 engine calls while a human thinks    | measured: ui.txt rewrites in 10 s, stopped 0, running + waiting for a human 17 before the fix, 0 after

# ---- the camera follows the human player (2026-11-08, owner: "cam should snap to entity esp p1") ----
# MECHANISM (proved with positive controls in the live editor): the default 3D camera (mode 2) sits behind the XELECTOR and the engine re-reads <editor>-pchq/pieces/xelector_01/state.txt pos_x/pos_y every frame it renders; a file write alone does NOT redraw: append one 126 to <bv_session>/pieces/apps/player_app/interact_relay.txt (bv_keys <session> '~').
# Writing selector_x/selector_y in bv_state.txt moves nothing (the old trap); camset pan values are relative to cam_home and do not follow the figure. A fresh editor launch has the cursor possessing hero_01 (pinned to the hero): the snap lets go of it like key 9.
NAV | camera | snap-on-turn    | deskopoly_driver, once per human turn (and once more 6 s after the first auto snap of a driver run, because a relaunch resets the cursor after the driver started) | only while the game runs; never during a pet's turn, never per tick
NAV | camera | find-me        | popup button `Find me` (id gmbN, last button; label stable)                | deskopoly_ctl find_me <games dir> is the same line; the answer text `camera: here is your figure` (or why not) stays 4 s
NAV | camera | aim            | cursor = figure cell + camera_lead (4) cells along the view direction     | aimed at the figure itself it hides behind the game popup (first live try); tuning.pdl rows camera_follow (0 = off, no button) and camera_lead
NAV | camera | guards         | AUTO snap (once per turn): free camera (mode 1/3/4), a cursor possessing something other than hero_01, no board session = nothing moves. EXPLICIT `Find me`: a free camera is NOT a reason to refuse (2026-11-09: it sets camera_mode=2, yaw 180, pitch 6, pan 0 like engine key 2, then snaps, answer `camera: following you again`); possession and no-session still refuse and the popup says why |
NAV | script | dsk-find-me    | tests/dsk-find-me.pdl     | presses Find me on the human's turn; shots 40 (before) 41 (after). WARNING: `in off` (every relay_drive script) lets the clock daemon run: see CPU pitfalls 33
NAV | case   | dsk_camera     | harness/cases/dsk_camera.pdl | 75 checks (2026-11-09: explicit Find me from mode 1/3, auto snap refuses a free camera in scenarios auto_free_3/auto_free_1) through the real driver with a fake board session and xelector (arithmetic, yaw, lead, guards each with a positive control, tuning off, turn change, pet turn does not move it); the PICTURE is judged in the live editor
NAV | case   | dsk_chathook   | harness/cases/dsk_chathook.pdl | 47 checks: the generic core hook (a real rpg_edit_hq.+x in a scratch house, the real engine, the 47-row fixture): typed offer writes the engine row as p1, refusals say why and write nothing, prose / no human seat / a book without the row / a missing program / a hung program (killed at 5 s) all behave as before, h-ai mode with a running game

# ---- the presentation video (2026-11-09; media in XO/31.Nov/nov-9/2.teropoly-presentation-video, never in the repo) ----
NAV | script | dsk-video-new     | tests/dsk-video-new.pdl     | New game button -> setup screen (then `deskopoly_ctl setup_reset <games dir>`); run live 2026-11-09, 5 steps passed
NAV | script | dsk-video-start   | tests/dsk-video-start.pdl   | setup: speed fast, you play p1, START GAME; 19 steps passed; pictures to /tmp/claude-1000/vid/raw
NAV | script | dsk-video-play    | tests/dsk-video-play.pdl    | the human turns of the recorded game (buy, skip + auction, trade); REASSEMBLED from blocks that each ran and passed alone, not run in one piece
NAV | script | dsk-video-typed   | tests/dsk-video-typed.pdl   | a trade TYPED in the table-talk box (`offer p2 give 100 get Orange3`): the pet answered `B rejected A's offer #2`; 9 steps passed
NAV | script | dsk-video-refused | tests/dsk-video-refused.pdl | a typed line the engine refuses (`offer p9 ...`): popup `chat: refused: name another player as the...`, ledger 60 rows before and after; 6 steps passed
NAV | fact   | typed-names       | the chat parser takes tile IDS (Orange3, Red1) or numbers (#19), NOT the on-screen labels (`Coil Plaza`, `CoilPlaza`, `coil` are refused as unknown names) | checked with `deskopoly_chat --parse` 2026-11-09; the table talk and popups show labels, the typed line needs ids
NAV | fact   | key-0-camera      | engine key `0` alone does NOT change camera_mode: 4 presses by bv_keys and 4 by the window relay (relay_drive key 0) left camera_mode=2 (observed 2026-11-09, render_mode 0,1,0,1). The engine key that sets camera_mode=1 is `1` (POV key: bv_menu_input.c is_pov_key writes camera_mode 1..4 and render_mode=1); a nav digit `1` (the tb-in number) sent while In: ON reaches the engine as that key | the earlier "four 0 presses left mode 1" note is NOT reproducible with key 0 alone; the likeliest cause is a stray `1` in the sequence (NOT proven: the earlier key log is gone). Not an engine bug found, engine not edited. `Find me` now recovers from any mode (see find-me)
NAV | fact   | talk-overlap      | FIXED 2026-11-09: each pane row is ONE fixed 30 px line (ov-scrolltext), so a 3-line sentence was drawn over the next. The driver now wraps every sentence to talk_wrap (24) characters and publishes each line as its own row gml_N_text with gml_N_cls alternating per sentence, at most talk_rows (16) rows (tuning.pdl) | case dsk_talkwrap (23); the shade needs the editor relaunched (xhtpm read at launch)

# ---- the second cut of the presentation video (2026-11-09; media in XO/31.Nov/nov-9/3.teropoly-presentation-video-v2, never in the repo) ----
NAV | script | dsk-video-findme  | tests/dsk-video-findme.pdl  | the REAL Find me button after the caller pressed the engine key `1` (`bv_keys <bv_session> 1`, camera_mode=1): popup `camera: following you again`, camera_mode back to 2; run twice live 2026-11-09, 7 steps passed each time
NAV | script | dsk-video-counter | tests/dsk-video-counter.pdl | in a STOPPED game with p2 current in PRE and an engine-CLI offer p2 -> p1 (`deskopoly.+x <app> <game dir> offer p1 give cash:20 get prop:26 as=p2`, then `ui`, then `deskopoly_ctl tr_close <games dir>`): Counter..., ask 10 more, Send counter, Amend offer..., ask 10 less, Send amendment, Cancel offer; 37 steps passed in one run, pictures 40 to 45
NAV | fact   | typed-labels-live | `offer p2 give 100 get Coil Plaza` typed in the table talk box works in the live window (2026-11-09): `A offered B: $100 for Coil Plaza (offer #2)`, `B rejected A's offer #2`; the typed `offer p9 ...` is still refused with the ledger unchanged (60 rows before and after) | supersedes the `typed-names` row above (ids only), which was true before the label fix the same day
NAV | fact   | say-by-id         | `tapid say`, NOT a pixel tap | the input row moves down as the table talk grows (y 366 with 5 rows, 516 with 9): the old `tap 1195 396` of dsk-video-typed.pdl missed it in the new wrapped layout
NAV | fact   | in-off-chat-focus | `STEP in off` FAILED once right after typing in the chat box (focus was in the input; the next `press label:...` then went to the game world with In: ON); running `in off` again alone passed | not reproduced twice, cause not proven; a script that follows typing should run `in off` as its own run first
NAV | fact   | video-frame-sizes | `video_op render` needs EVERY frame the same size | 2026-11-09: slides 1280x720 among screenshots 1280x790 gave a picture track of 278.72 s over 294.15 s of audio and squeezed the screenshots (the concat demuxer scales to the first frame); padding the slides to 1280x790 first (`ffmpeg -vf pad=1280:790:0:35:color=0x121622`) gave 294.16 s on both. video_op was not changed
NAV | fact   | dsk_camera-race   | case dsk_camera `find` failed 3 of 75 checks once (selector mirror, redraw nudge, nothing else) while cpu_gate waited at die temperature 87-89 C, and passed 75 of 75 alone on the rerun | the case reads the board session files right after a WAIT_HAS on the xelector file, which the driver writes a moment EARLIER than the mirror and the nudge: a race under load, not fixed
